===Etymology 1===
From {{compound|en|safety|valve|notext=1|type=exocentric}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=169691|date=March 2023}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=n|source=Random House}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[valve#Noun|valve]] [[set#Verb|set]] to [[open#Verb|open]] at a [[pressure#Noun|pressure]] below that at which a [[container]] [[hold#Verb|holding]] a [[gas#Noun|gas]], [[vapor#Noun|vapour]], etc. (such as a [[boiler]] or [[pressure cooker]]), would [[burst#Verb|burst]], thus [[reduce|reducing]] the pressure; a [[relief valve]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=British Locomotive Developments|magazine={{w|The Railway Magazine}}|location=London|publisher=Tothill Press|month=April|year=1941|page=173|issn=0033-8923|oclc=1256058197|passage=Spun glass mattresses are used for lagging the boiler, which has three Ross pop '''safety valves''' on the front ring.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Cecil J. Allen|authorlink=Cecil J. Allen|title=Locomotive Running Past and Present|magazine=[[w:Modern Railways|Trains Illustrated]]|location=London|publisher={{w|Ian Allan Publishing}}|month=April|year=1959|page=185|issn=0141-9935|oclc=35845948|passage=[A]nd to show that there was no shortage of steam, ''Royal Scot'', directly we stopped, blew off vigorously from its '''safety-valves''' steam that well might have been used in the cylinders in the interest of timekeeping.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A valve set to [[close#Verb|close]] a container holding a gas or vapour to [[prevent]] [[excessive]] [[loss#Noun|loss]] of pressure.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Any [[mechanism]] [[offer#Verb|offering]] [[relief#Noun|relief]] from [[physical#Adjective|physical]] or [[emotional]] pressure or [[tension#Noun|tension]].
#: {{synonyms|en|outlet|release}}
#* {{RQ:Marryat Olla Podrida|volume=I|chapter=XIX|pages=205–206|pageref=206|passage={{...}} I have often thought that it was a great error in our legislature when they consented to put down the public lotteries in England. I am convinced that they were beneficial, acting as '''safety-valves''' to the gambling spirit of the nation, and that their prohibition has been productive of much crime and misery.}}
## {{lb|en|US|law}} A [[United States]] [[law#Noun|law]], [[codify|codified]] at 18&nbsp;[[w:United States Code|United States Code]]&nbsp;§3553(f), [[authorize|authorizing]] a [[judge#Noun|judge]] to [[disregard#Verb|disregard]] [[mandatory#Adjective|mandatory]] [[minimum#Adjective|minimum]] [[sentence#Noun|sentences]] for some [[criminal#Noun|criminals]] with few or no [[prior#Adjective|prior]] [[offense]]s.
##* {{quote-journal|en|author={{w|David Jeremiah Barron}}, Circuit Judge, {{w|United States Court of Appeals for the First Circuit}}|title=United States v. Hernández-Hernández|series=No. 19-1123|journal=[[w:Federal Reporter|Federal Reporter{{nb...|Cases Argued and Determined in the United States Court of Appeals, United States Court of Claims, United States Court of Customs and Patent Appeals and Temporary Emergency Court of Appeals}}]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230702134744/https://casetext.com/case/united-states-v-hernandez-hernandez-62|location=St. Paul, Minn.|publisher=[[w:West (publisher)|West Publishing Co.]]|date=30 June 2020|volume=964|page=100|issn=1048-3888|oclc=891573999|passage=Hernández additionally requested that he be given a two-level '''safety-valve''' reduction pursuant to U.S.S.G. §&nbsp;5C1.2, which mitigates the harsh effect of mandatory minimum sentences on certain first-time offenders who played only supporting roles in drug-trafficking schemes and who provided testimony about their involvement in the criminal activity.|footer={{small|An {{glossary|attributive}} use.}}}}

